      "label": "(a)",
      "marks": 5,
      "answer": "$a=-\\frac{11}{3}$ and the intersection has position vector $12\\mathbf i-4\\mathbf j+4\\mathbf k$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Express a general point of at least one line correctly in component form — B1: $(1+a\\lambda,2+2\\lambda,1-\\lambda)$ or $(2+2\\mu,1-\\mu,-1+\\mu)$.\n\nEquate at least two pairs of corresponding components and solve for $\\lambda$ or $\\mu$ — M1, possibly implied; $1+a\\lambda=2+2\\mu$, $2+2\\lambda=1-\\mu$, $1-\\lambda=-1+\\mu$.\n\nObtain $\\lambda=-3$ or $\\mu=5$ — A1.\n\nObtain $a=-11/3$ — A1. Allow $a=-3.667$.\n\nState that the intersection has position vector $12\\mathbf i-4\\mathbf j+4\\mathbf k$ — A1. Allow coordinate form $(12,-4,4)$.\n\nTotal [5].",
